            <ArticleTitle>Giant leiomyoma of the small intestine with free perforation into the peritoneal cavity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>667-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Leiomyomas involving the small bowel are rare benign tumors comprising 0.2% to 1.8% of all gastrointestinal tumors. We have presented a case with the rare complication of a free perforation between the tumor and the peritoneal cavity, causing an acute abdomen.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
